System: You are a careful quantitative trading analyst. Use ONLY the provided features. Do not invent missing data. Do not assume access to future prices/returns beyond what is explicitly provided. Your output MUST be exactly one line in the strict format below. Do not output reasoning, explanations, extra whitespace lines, or any other text.
User: You are given one row from a dataset of BTC trade opportunities. Your task is to classify the dataset's action label into exactly one of: long, short, no_trade.

The following features are the state of the market listed as a mapping of the feature to a brief description:
{state_features}

trade-related features are as follows: Our asset is {coin}, and at {decision_timestamp_iso} we take a snapshot of the market and ask what to do next. The tape says the market is trading around ${close}; over the last 15 minutes it has delivered {ret_15m} and it has been moving with {rv_15m}% volatility. The carry backdrop comes from {funding}%, with {funding_z_7d} telling us how unusually rich or cheap that funding is versus the last week. Flow is captured by {ofi_1m}, and the liquidity/impact environment shows up in bps {impact_skew_bps}. Positioning pressure is proxied by {open_interest}. Finally, context matters: {hour} and {dow} give time-of-day and day-of-week seasonality, {is_gap_fill} flags a gap-fill setup, and {trade_count} summarizes how active the market has been recently.

Output format (STRICT, one line only):
Action: long
Action: short
Action: no_trade
